        Verse(chapter: 2, verse: "11",
              sanskrit: #"अशोच्यानन्वशोचस्त्वं प्रज्ञावादांश्च भाषसे ।\#nगतासूनगतासूंश्च नानुशोचन्ति पण्डिताः ॥"#,
              explanations: [
                .en: #"These are the first words of Krishna's teaching. Moments before the great war at Kurukshetra, Arjuna has seen his teachers, cousins and friends in the opposing army, thrown down his bow, and argued at length that fighting them would be a sin. Krishna gently points out the contradiction: Arjuna is speaking like a wise man while being ruled by grief. The wise, he says, do not mourn the living or the dead, because the true Self never dies. The lesson is to notice when our 'reasons' are really emotions in disguise, and to look at loss with a wider view."#,
              ],
