        Verse(chapter: 2, verse: "22",
              sanskrit: #"वासांसि जीर्णानि यथा विहाय नवानि गृह्णाति नरोऽपराणि ।\#nतथा शरीराणि विहाय जीर्णान्यन्यानि संयाति नवानि देही ॥"#,
              explanations: [
                .en: #"Continuing to explain why Arjuna need not grieve, Krishna gives a simple, homely image. Just as we take off worn-out clothes and put on new ones, the embodied Self leaves worn-out bodies and takes on new ones. It is one of the best-known pictures of rebirth in Indian thought. The lesson is that endings are also transitions: what is essential in us continues, even when its outer form changes."#,
              ],
              texts: [
