        Verse(chapter: 2, verse: "27",
              sanskrit: #"जातस्य हि ध्रुवो मृत्युर्ध्रुवं जन्म मृतस्य च ।\#nतस्मादपरिहार्येऽर्थे न त्वं शोचितुमर्हसि ॥"#,
              explanations: [
                .en: #"Having explained the Self, Krishna adds a plain, practical argument for the grieving Arjuna. Even if you just look at the facts, death is certain for everyone who is born, and birth follows death. Grieving over what cannot be avoided only adds to suffering. The lesson is acceptance: we can meet life's unavoidable realities with clarity instead of resisting them."#,
              ],
