        Verse(chapter: 2, verse: "28",
              sanskrit: #"अव्यक्तादीनि भूतानि व्यक्तमध्यानि भारत ।\#nअव्यक्तनिधनान्येव तत्र का परिदेवना ॥"#,
              explanations: [
                .en: #"Krishna asks Arjuna to look at life from a wider angle. Before birth, beings are unseen; after death, they are unseen again; only in between do they appear for a while. If that is the shape of every life, he asks, why grieve so bitterly over it? The lesson is perspective: our lives are a brief appearance between two mysteries, and seeing this can soften our sorrow over loss."#,
              ],
