        Verse(chapter: 2, verse: "29",
              sanskrit: #"आश्चर्यवत्पश्यति कश्चिदेनमाश्चर्यवद्वदति तथैव चान्यः ।\#nआश्चर्यवच्चैनमन्यः शृणोति श्रुत्वाप्येनं वेद न चैव कश्चित् ॥"#,
              explanations: [
                .en: #"Krishna admits that the Self is genuinely hard to grasp. Some see it as a marvel, some speak of it as a marvel, some hear of it as a marvel, and even after hearing, many do not understand it at all. He is not scolding Arjuna but being honest about how deep the subject is. The lesson is humility: the deepest truths are not understood by hearing alone, but by patient, lived realisation."#,
              ],
