        Verse(chapter: 2, verse: "40",
              sanskrit: #"नेहाभिक्रमनाशोऽस्ति प्रत्यवायो न विद्यते ।\#nस्वल्पमप्यस्य धर्मस्य त्रायते महतो भयात् ॥"#,
              explanations: [
                .en: #"Here Krishna moves from the philosophy of the Self to the practice of yoga, acting with a steady, unselfish mind. He reassures Arjuna that on this path no effort is ever wasted and no harm is done by trying. Even a little practice protects a person from great fear. The lesson is encouraging: you don't have to be perfect to begin, and every sincere step counts."#,
              ],
