        Verse(chapter: 2, verse: "41",
              sanskrit: #"व्यवसायात्मिका बुद्धिरेकेह कुरुनन्दन ।\#nबहुशाखा ह्यनन्ताश्च बुद्धयोऽव्यवसायिनाम् ॥"#,
              explanations: [
                .en: #"Krishna contrasts two kinds of mind. The resolute mind has one clear aim; the irresolute mind splinters into countless directions, each wanting something different. Arjuna, torn between duty and grief, is caught in exactly that scattering. The lesson is the power of focus: a single clear purpose gives strength, while a divided mind exhausts itself chasing many things at once."#,
