        Verse(chapter: 2, verse: "47",
              sanskrit: #"कर्मण्येवाधिकारस्ते मा फलेषु कदाचन ।\#nमा कर्मफलहेतुर्भूर्मा ते सङ्गोऽस्त्वकर्मणि ॥"#,
              explanations: [
                .en: #"This is perhaps the most famous verse of the Gita. Arjuna is paralysed because he is fixated on the terrible results the battle might bring. Krishna tells him his right is to his actions alone, never to their fruits, and that he should neither act for the sake of reward nor give up acting altogether. The lesson is to put your full effort into what is yours to do, and let go of anxiety about outcomes you cannot control."#,
              ],
              texts: [
