              ]),
        Verse(chapter: 2, verse: "48",
              sanskrit: #"योगस्थः कुरु कर्माणि सङ्गं त्यक्त्वा धनञ्जय ।\#nसिद्ध्यसिद्ध्योः समो भूत्वा समत्वं योग उच्यते ॥"#,
              explanations: [
                .en: #"Krishna is explaining to Arjuna how to act without being bound by action. He tells him to do his work grounded in yoga, free of attachment and equally balanced in success and failure. Then he gives one of the Gita's definitions of yoga: evenness of mind. The lesson is that yoga is not only a posture or a practice; it is staying steady whether things go your way or not."#,
              ],
              texts: [
