        Verse(chapter: 2, verse: "49",
              sanskrit: #"दूरेण ह्यवरं कर्म बुद्धियोगाद्धनञ्जय ।\#nबुद्धौ शरणमन्विच्छ कृपणाः फलहेतवः ॥"#,
              explanations: [
                .en: #"Krishna says that work done with craving for results is far inferior to work done with a calm, even mind. He goes further: those who act only for the reward are to be pitied, because their peace always depends on something outside their control. The lesson is that the spirit in which we act matters as much as the act itself, and that an even mind is a better refuge than any outcome."#,
              ],
              texts: [
