        Verse(chapter: 2, verse: "50",
              sanskrit: #"बुद्धियुक्तो जहातीह उभे सुकृतदुष्कृते ।\#nतस्माद्योगाय युज्यस्व योगः कर्मसु कौशलम् ॥"#,
              explanations: [
                .en: #"Krishna is continuing his teaching on acting with an even, unselfish mind. A person united with this wisdom, he says, rises above both good and bad deeds, so Arjuna should devote himself to yoga, which is 'skill in action'. The skill is in how we act: wholeheartedly, wisely, and without being chained to the results. The lesson is that spiritual life is not separate from work; it shows in the quality and spirit of everything we do."#,
              ],
              texts: [
