        Verse(chapter: 2, verse: "55",
              sanskrit: #"प्रजहाति यदा कामान् सर्वान् पार्थ मनोगतान् ।\#nआत्मन्येवात्मना तुष्टः स्थितप्रज्ञस्तदोच्यते ॥"#,
              explanations: [
                .en: #"Arjuna asks what a person of steady wisdom is like, and this is the first part of Krishna's answer. Such a person has let go of all the desires that pull at the mind and is content in the Self alone. They are not empty; they are full from within. The lesson is that true stability does not come from getting what we want, but from no longer needing it to be at peace."#,
              ],
