        Verse(chapter: 2, verse: "56",
              sanskrit: #"दुःखेष्वनुद्विग्नमनाः सुखेषु विगतस्पृहः ।\#nवीतरागभयक्रोधः स्थितधीर्मुनिरुच्यते ॥"#,
              explanations: [
                .en: #"Arjuna has just asked Krishna a very human question: what does a person with steady wisdom look like, and how do they speak, sit and walk? Krishna begins his famous portrait of the sthita-prajna, the person of stable mind. Such a person is not shaken by sorrow, does not crave pleasure, and is free from attachment, fear and anger. The lesson is that wisdom shows itself in emotional steadiness, not in clever words."#,
              ],
              texts: [
