        Verse(chapter: 2, verse: "58",
              sanskrit: #"यदा संहरते चायं कूर्मोऽङ्गानीव सर्वशः ।\#nइन्द्रियाणीन्द्रियार्थेभ्यस्तस्य प्रज्ञा प्रतिष्ठिता ॥"#,
              explanations: [
                .en: #"Krishna uses a simple image: a tortoise drawing its limbs into its shell. In the same way, the wise can draw the senses back from the things that attract them, and then their wisdom becomes steady. This is not about hating the world, but about being able to withdraw at will. The lesson is the value of being able to pull our attention back inward, instead of being dragged wherever the senses go."#,
              ],
              texts: [
